## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: Câu hỏi phỏng vấn

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Trả lời có ghi âm

**Câu hỏi tuần này:** *"Walk me through your release process."*

> *"There are three lanes, and which one a change takes depends on what it touches.*
> *Every pull request runs typecheck, lint, unit tests and a bundle size check against a written budget — four jobs in parallel, about ninety seconds. It also publishes a preview build and comments a QR code on the PR, so a reviewer can open the actual change on their phone instead of checking out the branch.*
> *Merging to main publishes an over-the-air update automatically. But the job refuses to run if the commit touched package.json or the app config, because OTA can only replace JavaScript. If you ship JavaScript that calls into native code that isn't in the installed binary, the app crashes on launch and the user can't fix it themselves.*
> *Store builds are deliberately manual — they're triggered by pushing a version tag. They cost build minutes, they go through review, and you can't roll them back the way you can roll back an update.*
> *End-to-end tests run nightly rather than per-PR. Maestro needs an emulator and takes several minutes, and a CI that takes twenty minutes per pull request is one people start working around.*
> *Main is protected, so none of this can be bypassed — including by me."*

**Câu cuối là câu hay nhất.** Nó nói rằng bạn hiểu quy trình tồn tại để bảo vệ cả người viết ra nó.

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lane` (n) | luồng, làn phát hành | *There are three lanes.* |
| `cut a build` | tạo một bản build | *Cut a build instead.* |
| `roll back` | quay lui phiên bản | *You can't roll them back easily.* |
| `work around` (v) | lách, đi vòng | *A CI people start working around.* |
| `bypass` (v) | bỏ qua quy trình | *None of this can be bypassed.* |

